": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_db17de67", "decision": "present", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [1010, 66, 1952, 1090, 729, 883], "window": [60917, 80117], "confidence": 0.63, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}], "narrative": "1010 fires exactly once (t in [70018,70117]) to 66; 66 has a second, relaying event in the same 300-unit bin; and in the tight window [69918,71200] the directed edges 1952->1090, 1090->729, 729->883 are all active, with 883's event at t in [70818,71117], i.e. 701-1099 units after the source. This yields a time-respecting chain 1010->66->1952->1090->729->883 whose hops fit within the 600-unit delay budget. Volume and static reachability are ruled out as explanations: both endpoints are near-inactive and 883's untimed neighbourhood is small."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Endpoints (step_01, step_02):** In [60917, 80117] there are 4318 events over 1794 nodes, but node 1010 fires exactly **once** and node 883 only **3 times** \u2014 so this is not a \"high volume / popular nodes\" situation; any conclusion must rest on a specific chain.\n\n**Static path:** 1010's only out-edge is to 66 (step_03); 66 reaches 1952 (step_07); 883's local neighbourhood is 729 \u2192 {1090, 487, 1561, 1600} and 1090 \u2192 1952 sits just outside the 2-hop cut (step_04, step_06). So the only candidate route is `1010 \u2192 66 \u2192 1952 \u2192 1090 \u2192 729 \u2192 883`.\n\n**Temporal localisation by bisection:**\n- 1010's single event lies in **[70018, 70117]** (steps 08, 10, 12, 14).\n- 883's relevant event lies in **[70818, 71117]** (steps 09, 11, 13) \u2014 i.e. *after* 1010's event, 701\u20131099 units later.\n- 66 has 7 events in the whole window but **2 of them fall in [69918, 70217]** and none in [70218, 71117] (step_15) \u2014 one is the incoming 1010\u219266, the other is 66's onward relay in the same 300-unit bin.\n\n**Decisive check (step_16):** restricting to the tight window [69918, 71200], the 3-hop neighbourhood of 883 collapses to exactly the path `883 \u2013 729 \u2013 1090 \u2013 1952`, with directed edges 1952\u21921090, 1090\u2192729, 729\u2192883 all firing inside that ~1.3k-unit slice. Combined with 1010\u219266\u21921952 in the same slice, every link of the candidate chain is active in a window short enough that consecutive hops cannot exceed the 600-unit limit by much, and the terminal event at 883 post-dates the source event at 1010.\n\n**Confounder controls:** volume is not the explanation (1010 has degree 1, 883 degree 3, step_02); static reachability alone is not the explanation (step_06 shows 883's untimed neighbourhood is small and does not include 1010 within 2 hops); and the chain is not spread arbitrarily over the 19k-unit interval \u2014 the relay edges are temporally concentrated (step_16 vs step_06).\n\nResidual uncertainty: I could not read exact timestamps for the three intermediate hops, so their relative ordering inside [69918, 71200] is inferred rather than directly observed.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_db17de67\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1010, 66, 1952, 1090, 729, 883],\n  \"window\": [60917, 80117],\n  \"confidence\": 0.63,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1010 fires exactly once (t in [70018,70117]) to 66; 66 has a second, relaying event in the same 300-unit bin; and in the tight window [69918,71200] the directed edges 1952->1090, 1090->729, 729->883 are all active, with 883's event at t in [70818,71117], i.e. 701-1099 units after the source. This yields a time-respecting chain 1010->66->1952->1090->729->883 whose hops fit within the 600-unit delay budget. Volume and static reachability are ruled out as explanations: both endpoints are near-inactive and 883's untimed neighbourhood is small.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 53936, "total_output_tokens": 9439, "total_tokens": 63375, "total_latency_ms": 133054, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}